# Normalize line endings for a cross-platform repository.
#
# The dev machine is Windows and CI runs on Linux. Without this, Git's
# `core.autocrlf` default can check files out as CRLF locally while the
# repository (and therefore CI) sees LF — producing whole-file diffs on every
# touch and making `git blame` useless.
#
# `eol=lf` stores LF and checks it out as LF on every platform, which is what
# the toolchain here expects (Vite, ESLint-style configs and the CDN all treat
# LF as canonical).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated verification output — never diff, never merge.
screenshots/** -text -diff

# Binary assets: keep bytes untouched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# pnpm owns this file; merging it by hand produces a broken tree.
pnpm-lock.yaml merge=binary
